-- title:
--   Switcheroo Aggregate First Term Eq Left Sandwich
-- statement:
--   **The first positive switcheroo term is a left-sandwich average.**
--
--   For a bipartite state, indexed polynomial family, and indexed projective submeasurement `M`, the named first aggregate term is exactly the uniform slice-question average of the left-sandwich expectation. If $G_x$ is the complete-part total at slice `x`, then
--
--   $$
--   \operatorname{switcherooAggregateFirstTerm}(\mathrm{params},\psi_{bi},\mathrm{family},M)
--   =\mathbb E_x\,\operatorname{leftSandwichExpectation}(\psi_{bi},M,G_x).
--   $$
--
--   The expectation uses the uniform distribution on slice questions. This rewrite exposes the first positive term in the form needed for the self-consistency transfer to the common middle-sandwich center.
--
--   Formalization credit: Sirui Lu, Ruixuan Deng, Yanqiao Zhu, and Zhengfeng Ji (arXiv:2609.19814). Mathematical source: Zhengfeng Ji, Anand Natarajan, Thomas Vidick, John Wright, and Henry Yuen (arXiv:2009.12982).
--
--   **Formalization Note.** The source declaration is `MIPStarRE.LDT.Pasting.switcherooAggregateFirstTerm_eq_leftSandwich`; its Lean statement gives the exact quantifier order and all boundary hypotheses.
